1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:02,280
=You Alone Know Me=

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:03,892
(From the Qimao novel "My Bestie's Icy
Dad Got Drunk and Wild After We Wed")

3
00:00:03,892 --> 00:00:04,920
(Written by Qiaoqiaojiang)

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:08,040
=Episode 23=

5
00:00:12,039 --> 00:00:12,720
Have a seat.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,640
Dinner's almost ready.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:14,800
Okay.

8
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:36,960
I picked this flower tea just for you.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:37,719
Try it.

10
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,479
(Sweet and tart, just how she likes it.)

11
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:54,079
Here.

12
00:00:56,359 --> 00:00:56,799
Try some.

13
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:19,159
With you staring at me,

14
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,439
I feel so...

15
00:01:22,359 --> 00:01:24,879
I'm just worried you won't like it.

16
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:26,719
It's delicious.

17
00:01:29,719 --> 00:01:31,640
You're good at compliments.

18
00:01:32,959 --> 00:01:35,159
You should give Bao'er more of them.

19
00:01:35,599 --> 00:01:37,439
Kids need encouragement.

20
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,359
It makes them confident and optimistic.

21
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:42,239
(I knew she'd plead Bao'er's case.)

22
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,799
No pressure, no diamonds.

23
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,120
With her personality,

24
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,719
too much praise will spoil her rotten.

25
00:01:52,439 --> 00:01:53,760
She just likes having fun.

26
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,640
She's kind and loyal

27
00:01:55,879 --> 00:01:56,920
to her family and friends,

28
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,040
and to me.

29
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,159
Besides, she's only a freshman.

30
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,319
Why push her so hard already?

31
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:04,159
Skip the hard lessons when you're young,

32
00:02:05,519 --> 00:02:06,560
and you'll learn them later.

33
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:12,719
You're such a good dad, Mr. Xie.

34
00:02:13,199 --> 00:02:14,719
You wouldn't force her to study, right?

35
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,599
I'm her best friend

36
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,039
and her stepmom.

37
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,919
Don't I get a say in her education?

38
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:27,400
When you put it that way, Mrs. Xie,

39
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:29,080
of course you do.

40
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,280
So,

41
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,719
is all this TOEFL prep

42
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,360
so she can study in the US?

43
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,240
She's always led a sheltered life.

44
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,400
And I know

45
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:43,639
spoiling her like this

46
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,319
will hurt her someday.

47
00:02:48,479 --> 00:02:49,599
I agree.

48
00:02:51,439 --> 00:02:52,280
But

49
00:02:52,639 --> 00:02:54,599
shouldn't we ask what she thinks?

50
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,560
Does she even want to go abroad?

51
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,759
I know you want what's best for her,

52
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:02,800
but

53
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:05,479
she'd be all alone out there,

54
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,639
with no one to look after her.

55
00:03:08,639 --> 00:03:09,560
It could be dangerous.

56
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,560
So I think

57
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:13,319
we should really think this through.

58
00:03:21,199 --> 00:03:22,479
All right, Mrs. Xie.

59
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:25,759
But at the very least,

60
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,879
she can't skip class again.

61
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,159
Deal.

62
00:03:29,639 --> 00:03:31,000
I'll make her put it in writing.

63
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:33,199
No more skipping class. Study hard.

64
00:03:34,039 --> 00:03:34,439
And

65
00:03:36,639 --> 00:03:37,719
no more wild nights out.

66
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,400
Especially with my wife.

67
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,360
You have my word.

68
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:45,599
You're such a good dad, Mr. Xie.

69
00:03:47,719 --> 00:03:48,400
Go on and eat.

70
00:03:49,159 --> 00:03:49,520
Here.

71
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:50,840
Try this.

72
00:03:55,039 --> 00:03:57,199
For the complex you see here,

73
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,000
(Architecture Meets Nature)
our core concept is breathing.

74
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:01,719
Buildings aren't sealed boxes.

75
00:04:01,919 --> 00:04:04,039
They should live and
breathe with the city.

76
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,400
On the east side,

77
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:08,039
we've added a public walkway
linking three floors

78
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,879
to let light and air flow through.

79
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,360
Here, we've designed...

80
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:13,000
Ms. Lin,

81
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,680
your proposal

82
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:17,279
is 20% over budget.

83
00:04:17,759 --> 00:04:19,199
In practice,

84
00:04:19,399 --> 00:04:20,199
it's unworkable.

85
00:04:20,759 --> 00:04:21,160
Ms. Xie,

86
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:23,519
I suggest sending it back for revision.

87
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,360
The excess cost

88
00:04:25,519 --> 00:04:26,839
mainly comes from the landscaping

89
00:04:26,959 --> 00:04:28,399
and renewable energy systems.

90
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,439
After three years,

91
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,439
these two systems

92
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,399
can achieve sustained cost savings.

93
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:33,600
The appendix includes

94
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,319
a detailed ten-year return projection.

95
00:04:41,639 --> 00:04:42,600
It passed the initial review.

96
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:43,759
Lin Hua,

97
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:44,879
next,

98
00:04:45,079 --> 00:04:46,600
you'll refine it with Wayne.

99
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,399
The final review is next week.

100
00:04:48,879 --> 00:04:49,279
Zhao Song,

101
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,600
double-check the budget.

102
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:52,560
That's all.

103
00:04:59,480 --> 00:04:59,959
Hua.

104
00:05:04,279 --> 00:05:04,839
Good proposal.

105
00:05:05,879 --> 00:05:06,720
But I think

106
00:05:07,399 --> 00:05:09,319
the east walkway's load-bearing beams

107
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:10,920
could use some more work.

108
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,720
Of course, Wayne.

109
00:05:26,879 --> 00:05:29,120
(Bao'er:)
(Great-Grandma set Dad up tonight.)

110
00:05:29,399 --> 00:05:30,920
(You'd better take this seriously.)

111
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,160
(The stuff I bought you)

112
00:05:36,199 --> 00:05:37,360
(has arrived at your apartment.)

113
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:38,279
(Check it, okay?)

114
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,439
(I told Dad)

115
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,319
(to come to your place tonight.)

116
00:05:47,319 --> 00:05:48,560
(You have to win him over!)

117
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,560
The form.

118
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,279
Yes, just do it like that.

119
00:06:11,759 --> 00:06:12,439
What are you doing?

120
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:14,160
Bao'er got you something.

121
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:16,480
She insisted I help you open it.

122
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,160
What is it?

123
00:06:44,533 --> 00:06:45,460
♪You say you♪

124
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:47,826
♪Don't need anyone♪
(Signature page, Party A Xie Zhouhan)

125
00:06:47,826 --> 00:06:50,600
♪You're just fine on your own♪

126
00:06:51,106 --> 00:06:53,690
♪I see the pride behind your smile♪

127
00:06:54,026 --> 00:06:56,610
♪And the pain you face at night♪

128
00:06:57,720 --> 00:07:00,210
♪Sometimes love isn't about possession♪

129
00:07:01,106 --> 00:07:03,660
♪It's tenderness that sets you free♪

130
00:07:03,906 --> 00:07:06,580
♪Some love needs no promises♪

131
00:07:06,853 --> 00:07:10,020
♪I'll face this cold world with you♪

132
00:07:10,266 --> 00:07:12,600
♪I keep my feelings safely hidden♪

133
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,810
♪Quietly staying behind you♪

134
00:07:16,506 --> 00:07:19,040
♪I'm right behind you♪

135
00:07:19,426 --> 00:07:22,410
♪Shielding you from every hidden storm♪

136
00:07:22,773 --> 00:07:25,010
♪Keeping the rain out of your eyes♪

137
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:29,000
♪So you can walk ahead without fear♪

138
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:35,210
♪I'm right behind you♪

139
00:07:35,853 --> 00:07:37,210
♪Waiting for you to turn around♪

140
00:07:37,293 --> 00:07:39,010
♪Waiting for you to finally see♪

141
00:07:39,213 --> 00:07:41,320
♪You're the only one I lose control for♪

142
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:43,026
♪I'm right behind you♪

143
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,480
♪Loving you gently, though no one knows♪

144
00:07:45,746 --> 00:07:47,210
♪I won't claim you♪

145
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:48,820
♪I won't ask you to stay♪

146
00:07:49,013 --> 00:07:51,480
♪I'll spend the rest of my life♪

147
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:54,826
♪Waiting for you♪
